supp=json.loads((R/'research/supplementary_assessments.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig'))
sa={'S020':'Collect two new willing replies: ask permission, ask each the same completed-years question, listen, record unique person letters and ages with units, then check each reply back. Private consenting actual people or an adult playing two different fictional people are valid; fictional replies supplied only after each question. Accurate conditional replies, not a fixed printed answer. Decline is accepted; never publish identifiable real ages. Score asking and recording separately from reading or table drawing.', 'S021':'With adult-approved full-size paper silhouettes, collect two NEW head-top observations: each labelled blank strip starts at the same floor baseline as that upright stand-in; mark each head level using the same method; align strip bottoms; compare and record both labels and taller/shorter/equal relationship. Real willing pupils require a safe consistent posture; do not compare sitting and standing stature or require John to stand. Accessible stand-ins are valid simulated collection, not actual child measurements. No resources means practical collection not assessed; picture interpretation alone is insufficient.'}
