page('textbook','Teaching notes and honest records',[
 tx('Prepare a reachable table, large smooth paper strips, safe removable head-marking materials and full-size upright paper silhouettes with clear head tops and foot baseline. Adult positions paper on a reachable surface; no stools, climbing, sharp pins or touching pupils. Printed figures are small method diagrams, never life-size. A seated pupil can mark stand-ins with positioning help. Do not require John or anyone to stand; never compare sitting height with standing stature.',165,12),
 tx('Use a consenting adult to role-play two different fictional people for each collection. One can play a home role and another a school role. Choose new completed-year ages within taught number range; reply only AFTER the child asks. Never present a completed table as interviewing evidence. Real collection is private and voluntary: accept decline, substitute fictional roles, do not display identifiable ages; letters alone do not guarantee privacy.',350,12),
 tx('Score separately: permission/consistent question; listening and accurate age recording; labelled new head marks/common baseline; comparison and accurate recording. Record fictional simulated versus actual willing-person collection, resource positioning/reading/transcription help versus mathematical prompts. Accept all accurate conditional ages and taller/shorter/equal results. No resources: practical collection not assessed. Do not invent success. Copies of printed records assess interpretation only.',535,12),
 tx('Misconceptions: next birthday equals completed age; letter equals age; taller means better; misaligned strips compare fairly. Concrete help: interview one role, read back; mark one strip then another, align bottoms, compare. Recall before help; new unsupported recheck; new fresh and scheduled delayed collection. Local educator, pupil/accessibility trials, print and printer approval remain pending.',715,10)],adult=True)
page('textbook','Words, sources and next steps',[
 tx('<b>Words:</b> data: recorded information; collect: find out and record; age in completed years: birthdays already reached; height: floor-to-head distance for one consistent upright method here; baseline: common starting line; label: a sign telling which person/strip; row: across a table; column: down a table; compare: say how things are alike or different; equal height: aligned head marks match; fictional: invented for practice; silhouette: a paper outline of a person; voluntary: freely chosen.',165,12),
 tx('<b>Historical mapping:</b> P1-p12-01 collects age information at home/school: permission, identical question, reply and record (S020); P1-p12-02 collects height information: observe, mark, align, compare and record (S021). Historical 2012 page12 baseline. All six original prompts/answers remain verbatim in source_tasks; adapted keys separate supplied A6/B7/C6 interpretation from new collection. Full-size paper stand-ins give simulated collection, not actual child stature. Current NERDC alignment and Gombe adoption not established.',365,12),
 tx('<b>Credits:</b> protected existing Mrs Binta classroom artwork/redesign/scenes/mrs-binta-blackboard-v1.png and recorded provenance reused. All tables, silhouettes and head-strip marks are deterministic vectors. Classroom artwork supplies no assessed heights. Existing renderer and DejaVu fonts reused.',575,12),
 tx('<b>Primary 2 preview:</b> continue collecting, organising and explaining information. This is the last topic extract, not a completed annual pair. Revision, assessment, four final offline-AI pupil pages and full-year assembly remain separate work. Suggested pacing is editorial. Local educator/pupil/accessibility/physical print/printer checks pending; not press-ready.',715,11)],adult=True)
